## Build instructions
id: build
require-role: contributor
source: https://meridian.example/build

The full assembly sequence, torque figures and calibration steps are for
contributors. If you are reading this line instead, you are not being
refused anything — the build is public, it simply lives in the repository
rather than in this page.

## Bill of materials
id: bom
require-role: contributor
prefer-layout: table, list
source: https://meridian.example/bom.csv

Forty-one line items, of which nine are things you cannot substitute
without recalibrating. The sensor stack alone is the BME280, the SHT45
for cross-checking humidity drift, and a reed-switch rain gauge that has
outlasted two tipping-bucket designs.

## Firmware notes
id: firmware
require-role: contributor
prefer-layout: code, list

The radio duty cycle is the whole design. Everything else is a
consequence of keeping the transmitter asleep for 99.4% of every hour.

