## Certification status
id: compliance
require-role: compliance
meta-valid-until: 2027-03-01
source: https://meridian.internal/compliance

Radio conformance, ingress-protection test results and the EMC report.
The `meta-valid-until` on this section is not decoration: after that date
a consumer should stop treating these results as current, because the
certificate behind them expires.

## Open questions
id: questions

Three things we have not settled. Whether the rain gauge should be
serviceable without opening the main enclosure. Whether five years is
honest or optimistic for the cell. And whether a second radio is worth
the power budget in valleys where the gateway is intermittent.

---

## How to read this page

Look at the same page four ways using the bar at the foot of it.

The structure view shows every section, its attributes grouped by family,
and whether this consumer implements the tag or is falling back. The
sections marked as falling back are doing exactly what the format
promises: showing you the sentence the author wrote for a reader who
cannot get the real thing.

The memo view shows the text this page was written in — including the
`require-role` lines, because who may see a section is not itself a
secret. The gate is public; what it guards is not.

The JSON view is what a consuming site actually receives.

## Watching one part of it
id: watching
ref: #specs

Every section above with an `id` can be watched on its own. Ask for
`?ref=specs` and you are told nothing has changed until that section
changes — not when the photographs are updated, not when a supplier price
moves, not when this paragraph is rewritten.

That is the whole subscription mechanism: no account, no registration, no
delivery owed to anyone. Ask again later and be told 304.
